course: dictionary
lesson: 8888
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists these as numbered meanings. «Shredder» is a noun, so it names a thing or a person. The words around it show which meaning is being used.
explain: A paper shredder is a machine that cuts paper into thin strips so no one can read it. «A shredder's blades can catch fingers, hair, ties and sleeves; many have a slot too thin for a small child's fingers, and children do not use one alone.» Blades, fingers and safety are the clues that tell you it is a machine.
explain: Slang is informal talk that people use with friends. «He's a total shredder on the guitar» does not mean a machine at all. It means he plays very fast and skilled guitar. When a word seems odd in a sentence, ask yourself: could this be a different meaning?
fact: A noun is a naming word for a person, place or thing.
fact: «Shredder» means a machine that cuts paper into thin strips so it cannot be read.
fact: A shredder can also be a kitchen tool or machine part that cuts food or other things into thin pieces.
fact: Slang is everyday, informal talk: «shredder» can mean a very skilled guitar player, or a brilliant surfer or snowboarder.
fact: Keep fingers, hair and ties away from a shredder, and never feed it when it is jammed.
exercise: «A shredder's blades can catch fingers, hair, ties and sleeves.» What is a shredder in this sentence? | A soft, warm blanket | *A machine with blades that cuts things into thin pieces | A slow, quiet guitar player | A kind of snowboard
exercise: Why do grown-ups shred letters with names and bank details? | To make the letters longer | *To protect against identity theft | To turn the letters into a kite | To make the paper easier to read
exercise: «He's a total shredder on the guitar.» What does shredder mean here? | A machine for cutting paper | *A very fast, skilled guitar player | A person who sweeps floors | A kitchen tool for food
test: What is the safety rule for a paper shredder? | *Never feed it when it is jammed, and keep fingers away | Feed it paper while it is jammed | Use it on your own when you are small | Put your fingers in the slot to clear a jam
test: Shredded paper can be used as what? | A shiny bell | Food for hamsters | A kite for the summer | *Bedding for hamsters
exam: How can you tell which meaning of shredder is used in a sentence? | Ask the shredder itself | Skip the word forever | *Read the words around it for clues, then check your meaning makes sense | Guess the first meaning you think of
